[38;5;252m[1m### Bug Found & Fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mSign-extension bug in [38;5;10mstbds_siphash_bytes[0m main loop[22m ([38;5;10msrc/lib.rs[0m):[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The C code assembles 8-byte [38;5;10mdata[0m values from individual bytes using [38;5;10md[0] | (d[1] << 8) | (d[2] << 16) | (d[3] << 24)[0m. In C, [38;5;10munsigned char[0m promotes to [38;5;10mint[0m before shifting. When [38;5;10md[3] >= 0x80[0m, [38;5;10md[3] << 24[0m produces a negative [38;5;10mint[0m, which sign-extends when OR'd into [38;5;10msize_t[0m. The same applies to the high 32 bits with [38;5;10md[7][0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The original Rust code cast each byte directly to [38;5;10musize[0m before shifting, which doesn't sign-extend. Fixed by computing the low and high 32-bit halves as [38;5;10mi32[0m first (matching C's [38;5;10mint[0m promotion), then casting to [38;5;10musize[0m:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mrust
[0m[38;5;10m// Before (wrong):
data = *dp.add(0) as usize | (*dp.add(1) as usize) << 8 | ...

// After (correct):
let lo = (*dp.add(0) as i32) | (*dp.add(1) as i32) << 8 | ... ;
data = lo as usize;
[0m[0m[0m
